        </div>
        <div class='list-authors'><a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Githinji,+P+B">P. Bilha Githinji</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Melliou,+A">Aikaterini Melliou</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Liang,+Z">Zeming Liang</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+L">Lian Zhang</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Qin,+P">Peiwu Qin</a></div>

        <div class='list-comments mathjax'><span class='descriptor'>Comments:</span>
          NLP4DH 2026 Open review page at <a href="https://openreview.net/forum?id=GutmBiDoRR" rel="external noopener nofollow" class="link-external link-https">this https URL</a> . In a nutshell, to achieve better generalizability, we need to soften the language and/or expand the number of models and document classes under review. As it is right now, the analysis only speaks to biomedical text and two models (QWen 2.5 and Mistral-small). We acknowledge this as a limitation and area for future work
